  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "Chef is cooking his finest dish yet. The recipe calls for a series of NNN steps, where the iii-th step is recommended to be performed at a temperature of AiA_iAi​.\n\nThe steps must be performed in order from 111 to NNN.\n\nThe further away from the recommended temperature Chef gets, the worse the dish tastes.\n\nSuppose Chef performs the iii-th step at a temperature of BiB_iBi​.\n\nThe unsavoriness of the dish is then defined to be\n\nmax⁡i=1N∣Ai−Bi∣\\max_{i=1}^N |A_i - B_i|i=1maxN​∣Ai​−Bi​∣That is, the unsavoriness is the maximum temperature difference across all the steps.\n\nNote that ∣x∣|x|∣x∣ refers to the absolute value of xxx.\n\nChef can choose to perform each step at any temperature he wishes - i.e. he can choose the array BBB freely.\n\nHowever, he doesn't want to change the temperature too often from one step to the next.\n\nA temperature change happens at step iii (where 2≤i≤N2 \\leq i \\leq N2≤i≤N) if Bi≠Bi−1B_i \\neq B_{i-1}Bi​=Bi−1​.\n\nFor example, if B=[1,1,2,2,6,3]B = [1, 1, 2, 2, 6, 3]B=[1,1,2,2,6,3], there are three temperature changes: at steps 3,5,3, 5, 3,5, and 666.\n\nYou are the given the array AAA denoting recommended temperatures.\n\nIf Chef can choose the array BBB freely, and change temperature **at most** KKK times from one step to the next, what's the **minimum** possible unsavoriness of the dish?\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nEach test case consists of two lines of input.\n\nThe first line of each test case contains two space-separated integers NNN and KKK — the number of steps in the recipe and the maximum allowed number of temperature changes, respectively.\nThe second line contains NNN space-separated integers A1,A2,…,ANA_1, A_2, \\ldots, A_NA1​,A2​,…,AN​, the recommended  temperature of the NNN steps.\n\n\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output on a new line one integer: the minimum possible unsavoriness.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1051 \\leq T \\leq 10^51≤T≤105",
      "1≤N≤2⋅1051 \\leq N \\leq 2\\cdot 10^51≤N≤2⋅105",
      "0≤K≤N0 \\leq K \\leq N0≤K≤N",
      "1≤Ai≤1091 \\leq A_i \\leq 10^91≤Ai​≤109",
      "The sum of NNN over all test cases won't exceed 2⋅1052\\cdot 10^52⋅105."
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
